commit b58965be887928c9521b34affbe3ff22703aca43
Author: Ben Mattes Krusekamp <ben.krause05@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 15 18:37:07 2022 +0200

    Addition of 64-bit Rasberry Pi OS support
    
    In the current version of the driver, the pointer length of "Source_Buffer_Addr" is hardcoded as UDOUBLE (uint32_t),
    meaning the use of a non-32-bit OS will result in a Segmentation fault.
    This is why I have changed the type to UBYTE* (uint8_t*).
    As this address is used only internally, the existing code will still work.

